  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As I understand it, IPD is calculated with the arm span of the user's avatar. This allows the arm span of the avatar to match the user's arm span, and is probably the most desirable behavior for IPD calculation, so I won't dispute this decision.\n\nHowever, many user avatars have stylized proportions, which often places the virtual floor under the user's physical floor, making it impossible or nigh-impossible to pick up objects that have fallen onto the virtual floor.\n\nSpecial consideration -- perhaps simply increasing the detection radius when the player reaches low enough -- could be made for objects that fall under the player's physical floor, to make it possible to easily pick them up without external tools like OpenVR-AdvancedSettings's playspace manipulation.",
